mermaid:
flowchart TD
A["Ticket arrives in FW-Changes queue (oldest first unless EMERGENCY)"] --> B{Form complete? src, dest, port/proto, justification, named system owner}
B -->|No| C["Kick back to requester with note of what is missing; status Waiting on Requester"]
C --> D{Requester replies within 5 business days?}
D -->|Yes| A
D -->|No| E["Ticket auto-closes as Abandoned"]
B -->|Yes| F{Expiry field blank?}
F -->|Yes| G["Default expiry to 90 days"]
F -->|No| H{Any/any request?}
G --> H
H -->|Yes| I["Reject and close with standard 'not permitted by policy' reply"]
H -->|No| J{Destination external?}
J -->|No, internal| M["Score using risk sheet"]
J -->|Yes| K{On threat intel blocklist?}
K -->|Yes| L["Reject, close ticket, tell requester why, and notify SOC channel"]
K -->|No| M
M --> N{Score 7 or above?}
N -->|No, under 7| P["Approve yourself"]
N -->|Yes| O["Send to security architect"]
O --> Q{Architect decision}
Q -->|Approve| P
Q -->|Deny| R["Close ticket with architect's reason in reply to requester"]
Q -->|Request changes| C
P --> S{Tagged EMERGENCY and manager approved tag in ticket?}
S -->|No| T["Schedule in next change window (Tue or Thu night)"]
S -->|Yes| U["Skip change window and implement right away"]
T --> V["On the night: stage rule in policy manager, push it, run connectivity test with requester on a call"]
U --> V
V --> W{Test passes?}
W -->|Yes| X["Tag rule in policy manager with ticket number and expiry date"]
X --> Y["Notify requester and close ticket"]
Y --> Z{Was it an emergency implementation?}
Z -->|No| END["End"]
Z -->|Yes| AA["File retroactive CAB record within 24 hours"]
AA --> AB{CAB rejects retroactively?}
AB -->|Yes| AC["Rule is pulled"]
AB -->|No| END
W -->|No| AD["Roll back immediately"]
AD --> AE["Check with network team what went wrong, fix and retry once"]
AE --> AF{Retry passes?}
AF -->|Yes| X
AF -->|No| AG["Roll back again, mark ticket Failed Implementation, escalate to network eng lead, tell requester it is escalated; do not close"]
